import VOA.Modules.ZhuVermaAnArchDJAction
import VOA.Modules.ZhuVermaAnArchRightUnit

/-!
# Dong–Jiang Theorem 4.10's generation clause: `M(U)` is generated by its level-`m` piece

Dong–Jiang, *Bimodules associated to vertex operator algebras*, Math. Z. 259 (2008) 799–826
(`math/0601626`), prove their main construction theorem (printed Theorem 4.10) in a paragraph whose
**first sentence** is the entire generation argument:

> "Since `u ∗̄ⁿ_m 1 = u`, for `u ∈ V` and `1 ∈ A_m(V)`, it follows that `M(U)` is generated by
> `U ≅ A_{m,m}(V) ⊗_{A_m(V)} U` by Proposition `pa4.5`."

That is **one line, not an induction**, and this file ports it as one line.  The two ingredients are

1. a **unit law** for the level-changing product against the vacuum, and
2. DJ **Proposition `pa4.5`** (printed Prop. 4.6), `A_{m,m}(V) = A_m(V)`, which is what turns the
   level-`m` piece into `U`.

Everything is stated on the genuine Dong–Jiang carrier of `ZhuVermaAnArchDJCarrier`/`…Graded` —
the **balanced** tensor `M(U)(n) = A_{n,m}(𝒱) ⊗_{A_m(𝒱)} U` over the **full** ideal
`A_{n,m}(𝒱) = 𝒱 ⧸ O_{n,m}(𝒱)`, at **general** base level `m` — with the modes of
`ZhuVermaAnArchDJAction`.

## §1–§3  The vacuum in the RIGHT slot of `∗^N_{m,p}`, at general base level `m`

The engine is the exact mirror of `anmGen_vacuum_scalar` (`ZhuVermaAnArchDJAction` §4, which puts
the vacuum in the LEFT slot).  Working in `A_{N,m}(𝒱)`, the shifted grading relation
`L₋₁x + (L₀ + m − N)x ∈ O'_{N,m}` gives `[x₍μ₎𝟙] = C(−(k+m−N), −μ−1)·[x]` for `x ∈ 𝒱_k`
(`mkAnmFull_smul_vacuum_homog`), the generalized-binomial Vandermonde collapses each residue to
`[Res_z (1+z)^{k+m} z^{−P} Y(x,z)𝟙] = C(N, P−1)·[x]` (`mkAnmFull_resHom_vacuum`), and a second
Vandermonde — after `cbz_neg_upper` and `ZhuMu.cbz_symm`, exactly as in
`anmGen_vacuum_scalar` — collapses the outer `i`-sum:

  `[u ∗^N_{m,p} 𝟙] = C(p − m − 1, p − m) · [u]`  in `A_{N,m}(𝒱)`,  for **every** `u : 𝒱`,

`mkAnmFull_anmGen_vacuum_right`.  The scalar does not depend on the target level `N`.  Two
specializations:

* `p = m` (the right `A_m(𝒱)`-action `∗^N_m`): the scalar is `C(−1,0) = 1`, i.e. the **unit law**
  `mkAnmFull_anmRight_vacuum_right : [u ∗^N_m 𝟙] = [u]`.  This is the identity DJ's sentence
  uses.
* `p = N` (the left `A_N(𝒱)`-action `∗̄^N_m`): the scalar is `C(N − m − 1, N − m) = δ_{N,m}`, i.e.
  `mkAnmFull_anmGenBar_vacuum_diag : [u ∗̄^m_m 𝟙] = [u]` but
  `mkAnmFull_anmGenBar_vacuum_offdiag : [u ∗̄^N_m 𝟙] = 0` for `N ≠ m`.

⚠ **Source note (a typo in DJ, not a divergence here).**  DJ's sentence writes `∗̄ⁿ_m`, but
`u ∗̄ⁿ_m 𝟙 = u` is *false* for `n ≠ m` — `mkAnmFull_anmGenBar_vacuum_offdiag` proves the left-hand
side is `0`.  DJ's own parenthetical "`1 ∈ A_m(V)`" identifies `𝟙` as the identity of the *algebra*
`A_m(V)`, i.e. as the element of the RIGHT slot of `∗ⁿ_m = ∗^n_{m,m}` (which is precisely the
product DJ define as inducing the right `A_m(V)`-module structure), not of the module slot of
`∗̄ⁿ_m = ∗^n_{m,n}`.  With `∗ⁿ_m` the sentence is correct and is what generation needs: it is the
mode carrying level `m` to level `n`.  So the correct reading is `u ∗ⁿ_m 𝟙 = u`, proved here.

## §4  Generation

`DJModeStable W U hD S` says a `ℂ`-subspace `S ⊆ M(U)` is stable under every Dong–Jiang mode
`u_p` — i.e. `S` is a `𝒱`-submodule of `M(U)`.  The generation statement is then

`djCarrier_generated_by_degM` : a mode-stable `S` with `M(U)(m) ⊆ S` is all of `M(U)`,

with the sharper, hypothesis-light `djCarrier_generated_by_vacTensor` behind it (it is enough that
`S` contains the single family `𝟙 ⊗ w`, `w ∈ U`).  The proof is DJ's one line: an element of
`M(U) = ⨁ₙ M(U)(n)` is a finite sum of level vectors `[v] ⊗ w`, and

  `v_{wt v − 1 + m − n} (𝟙 ⊗ w) = (v ∗ⁿ_{m,m} 𝟙) ⊗ w = (v ∗ⁿ_m 𝟙) ⊗ w = [v] ⊗ w` .

**No induction on the level is used** — one mode application reaches level `n` from level `m`
directly.  (This is the point of DJ's carrier: on a `⊗_ℂ`-carrier one is forced into a "level
reach" induction, which DJ do not have.)

`djCarrier_degM_le_span` records, **unconditionally**, that `M(U)(m)` is already spanned by the
vectors `𝟙 ⊗ w`: the sharp Frenkel–Zhu unit `𝟙 ∗^m_m x = x` (`anmRight_diag_vacuum_left`) plus the
balancing gives `[x] ⊗ w = 𝟙 ⊗ ρ([x])w`.  So the generation theorem needs **no** hypothesis beyond
the mode descent `DJActionDescent W m` (which is a theorem at `m = 0`,
`djCarrier_generated_by_degZero`).

## §5  DJ's own phrasing (this is where Prop. 4.6 enters)

`djCarrier_generated_by_U` is DJ's sentence verbatim: given `DJAnnEqAn W m` (= DJ Prop. `pa4.5`
`A_{m,m}(𝒱) = A_m(𝒱)`, carried as an explicit named hypothesis — DJ prove it by invoking
**Dong–Li–Mason III Theorem 4.1**, which is not available in this repo, and give no combinatorial
proof), `M(U)` is generated by the image of `U` under `DJCarrier.degMEquiv`.

## What is hypothesis, exactly

* `hD : DJActionDescent W m` — DJ Lemma 2.8's left inclusion, needed for the modes to exist at all.
  Unconditional at `m = 0` (`djActionDescent_zero`).
* `h : DJAnnEqAn W m` — DJ Prop. `pa4.5`.  Needed **only** for the `U`-phrasing of §5, not for the
  generation theorem itself.

Nothing else.  Axiom-clean (`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]`), `sorry`-free, `pbw`-free.

## References
Dong–Jiang, Math. Z. 259 (2008) 799–826 (`math/0601626`), §2 (the products `∗^n_{m,p}`, `∗ⁿ_m`,
`∗̄ⁿ_m`; `O'_{n,m}`), §4 (`M(U)`, Prop. `pa4.5`, Thm 4.10); Dong–Li–Mason, J. Algebra 206 (1998)
67–96 (DLM3, Thm 4.1).
Repo: `ZhuVermaAnArchAnmFull` (`anmGen`, `anmGenBar`, `OnmFull`, `AnmFull`),
`ZhuVermaAnArchDJCarrier` (`DJPiece`, `mkDJPiece_balance`, `anmRight_diag_vacuum_left`,
`DJAnnEqAn`), `ZhuVermaAnArchDJCarrierGraded` (`DJCarrier`, `DJCarrier.deg`,
`DJCarrier.degMEquiv`), `ZhuVermaAnArchDJAction` (`djMode`, `djMode_apply_tmul`,
`anmGen_vacuum_scalar`), `ZhuVermaAnArchRightUnit` (`Tpow_mem_grading`, the diagonal right-unit
technique this file generalizes off the diagonal), `ZhuRingResidue` (`ZhuRes.vandermonde_range`,
`reduce_homogeneous`), `ZhuMuIdentity` (`ZhuMu.cbz_symm`), `ZhuVermaAnArchDJ48` (`cbz_neg_upper`).
-/

namespace VOA

open VertexOperatorAlgebra
open scoped BigOperators TensorProduct DirectSum

universe u

variable {𝒱 : Type u} [AddCommGroup 𝒱] [Module ℂ 𝒱]

/-! ## §1 The `O'_{N,m}`-coset calculus for translates in `A_{N,m}(𝒱)`

The level-`(N,m)` analogue of the diagonal calculus of `ZhuVermaAnArchRightUnit`.  The only change
is the Dong–Jiang **shift**: the grading generator of `O'_{N,m}` is `L₋₁u + (L₀ + m − N)u`, so the
coset relation carries the extra `m − N`. -/

/-- The Dong–Jiang grading generator vanishes in `A_{N,m}(𝒱) = 𝒱 ⧸ O_{N,m}(𝒱)`. -/
theorem mkAnmFull_anmLgen_eq_zero (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m : ℕ) (x : 𝒱) :
    mkAnmFull W N m (anmLgen W N m x) = 0 := by
  rw [mkAnmFull, Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
  exact anmLgen_mem_OnmFull W N m x

/-- **Translate coset (homogeneous), shifted.**  For `x ∈ 𝒱_w`,
`[L₋₁ x] = −(w + m − N)·[x]` in `A_{N,m}(𝒱)`. -/
theorem mkAnmFull_L_neg_one_homog (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m : ℕ) {w : ℤ} {x : 𝒱}
    (hx : x ∈ W.grading w) :
    mkAnmFull W N m (W.L (-1) x)
      = (-((w : ℂ) + (m : ℂ) - (N : ℂ))) • mkAnmFull W N m x := by
  have h0 := mkAnmFull_anmLgen_eq_zero W N m x
  rw [anmLgen, map_add, map_add, W.L_zero_grading x hx, map_smul, map_smul, add_assoc,
    ← add_smul] at h0
  have h1 : mkAnmFull W N m (W.L (-1) x)
      = -(((w : ℂ) + ((m : ℂ) - (N : ℂ))) • mkAnmFull W N m x) := by
    rw [eq_neg_iff_add_eq_zero]; exact h0
  rw [h1, ← neg_smul]
  congr 1
  ring

/-- `T`-form of the shifted translate coset (`T = L₋₁`). -/
theorem mkAnmFull_T_homog (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m : ℕ) {w : ℤ} {x : 𝒱}
    (hx : x ∈ W.grading w) :
    mkAnmFull W N m (W.toPreVertexAlgebra.T x)
      = (-((w : ℂ) + (m : ℂ) - (N : ℂ))) • mkAnmFull W N m x := by
  rw [show W.toPreVertexAlgebra.T x = W.L (-1) x from by rw [T_eq_Lneg1]]
  exact mkAnmFull_L_neg_one_homog W N m hx

/-- **Iterated shifted translate coset.**  For `a ∈ 𝒱_k`,
`[Tᵗ a] = (∏_{s<t}(−(k + m − N + s)))·[a]` in `A_{N,m}(𝒱)`. -/
theorem mkAnmFull_Tpow_homog (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m : ℕ) {k : ℤ} {a : 𝒱}
    (ha : a ∈ W.grading k) (t : ℕ) :
    mkAnmFull W N m ((W.toPreVertexAlgebra.T ^ t) a)
      = (∏ s ∈ Finset.range t, (-((k : ℂ) + (m : ℂ) - (N : ℂ) + (s : ℂ))))
          • mkAnmFull W N m a := by
  induction t with
  | zero => simp
  | succ t ih =>
      rw [pow_succ', Module.End.mul_apply,
        mkAnmFull_T_homog W N m (Tpow_mem_grading W ha t), ih, smul_smul,
        Finset.prod_range_succ]
      push_cast
      ring_nf

/-- **Mode-on-vacuum coset, shifted.**  For `a ∈ 𝒱_k` and any mode `μ`,
`[a₍μ₎𝟙] = C(−(k + m − N), −μ−1)·[a]` in `A_{N,m}(𝒱)`. -/
theorem mkAnmFull_smul_vacuum_homog (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m : ℕ) {k : ℤ} {a : 𝒱}
    (ha : a ∈ W.grading k) (μ : ℤ) :
    mkAnmFull W N m (W.smul a μ W.vacuum)
      = cbz (-(k + (m : ℤ) - (N : ℤ))) (-μ - 1) • mkAnmFull W N m a := by
  rcases lt_or_ge μ 0 with hμ | hμ
  · obtain ⟨t, rfl⟩ : ∃ t : ℕ, μ = -(t : ℤ) - 1 := ⟨(-μ - 1).toNat, by omega⟩
    rw [show -(-(t : ℤ) - 1) - 1 = (t : ℤ) from by ring]
    rw [cbz_apply_nonneg (-(k + (m : ℤ) - (N : ℤ))) (by omega),
      show (t : ℤ).toNat = t from by omega]
    rw [creation_pow W a t, map_smul, mkAnmFull_Tpow_homog W N m ha t, smul_smul]
    congr 1
    rw [gBinom]
    rw [eq_div_iff (by exact_mod_cast Nat.factorial_ne_zero t)]
    rw [mul_comm, ← mul_assoc]
    rw [mul_inv_cancel₀ (by exact_mod_cast Nat.factorial_ne_zero t : ((t.factorial : ℂ)) ≠ 0)]
    rw [one_mul]
    refine Finset.prod_congr rfl fun s _ => ?_
    push_cast; ring
  · rw [PreVertexAlgebra.smul_vacuum_nonneg _ _ hμ, map_zero,
      cbz_apply_neg (-(k + (m : ℤ) - (N : ℤ))) (by omega), zero_smul]

/-! ## §2 A top-truncated generalized-binomial Vandermonde -/

/-- **Top-truncated Vandermonde.**  For `A ≥ 0` (so `C(A,i)` vanishes above `i = A`),
`∑_{i ≤ A} C(A,i)·C(B, c−i) = C(A+B, c)`.  Extends `ZhuRes.vandermonde_range` past the range
`[0,c]` by discarding the vanishing top terms. -/
theorem cbz_vandermonde_top (A : ℤ) (hA : 0 ≤ A) (B c : ℤ) :
    (∑ i ∈ Finset.range (A.toNat + 1), cbz A (i : ℤ) * cbz B (c - (i : ℤ)))
      = cbz (A + B) c := by
  have hsub : Finset.range (A.toNat + 1) ⊆ Finset.range (A.toNat + 1 + c.toNat + 1) := by
    intro i hi
    simp only [Finset.mem_range] at hi ⊢
    omega
  have hzero : ∀ i ∈ Finset.range (A.toNat + 1 + c.toNat + 1),
      i ∉ Finset.range (A.toNat + 1) → cbz A (i : ℤ) * cbz B (c - (i : ℤ)) = 0 := by
    intro i _ hi
    rw [Finset.mem_range, not_lt] at hi
    rw [cbz_lt hA (by omega), zero_mul]
  rw [Finset.sum_subset hsub hzero,
    ZhuRes.vandermonde_range A B c (N := A.toNat + 1 + c.toNat + 1) (by omega)]

/-! ## §3 The vacuum in the RIGHT slot of the Dong–Jiang products, at general base level `m` -/

/-- `Res_z (1+z)^{wt · + m} z^{−P} Y(0,z)v = 0` (linearity in the left slot). -/
private theorem resHom_zero_left_dj (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (s P : ℤ) (v : 𝒱) :
    resHom W s P 0 v = 0 := by
  have h := resHom_smul_left W s P (0 : ℂ) 0 v
  simp only [zero_smul] at h
  exact h

/-- **The vacuum residue in the right slot**, for homogeneous `a ∈ 𝒱_k`:
`[Res_z (1+z)^{k+m} z^{−P} Y(a,z)𝟙] = C(N, P−1)·[a]` in `A_{N,m}(𝒱)`.  Each mode contributes
`C(k+m, i)·C(−(k+m−N), P−1−i)`, and the top-truncated Vandermonde collapses the `i`-sum. -/
theorem mkAnmFull_resHom_vacuum_homog (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m : ℕ) (P : ℤ)
    {k : ℤ} {a : 𝒱} (ha : a ∈ W.grading k) :
    mkAnmFull W N m (resHom W (m : ℤ) P a W.vacuum)
      = cbz (N : ℤ) (P - 1) • mkAnmFull W N m a := by
  rcases lt_or_ge k 0 with hk | hk
  · have ha0 : a = 0 := by
      have hbot : a ∈ (⊥ : Submodule ℂ 𝒱) := W.positivity k hk ▸ ha
      simpa using hbot
    subst ha0
    simp only [resHom_zero_left_dj, map_zero, smul_zero]
  rw [resHom_homogeneous W (m : ℤ) P ha W.vacuum, map_sum]
  have hterm : ∀ i ∈ Finset.range ((k + (m : ℤ)).toNat + 1),
      mkAnmFull W N m (cbz (k + (m : ℤ)) (i : ℤ) • W.smul a ((i : ℤ) - P) W.vacuum)
        = (cbz (k + (m : ℤ)) (i : ℤ)
            * cbz (-(k + (m : ℤ) - (N : ℤ))) ((P - 1) - (i : ℤ))) • mkAnmFull W N m a := by
    intro i _
    rw [map_smul, mkAnmFull_smul_vacuum_homog W N m ha ((i : ℤ) - P),
      show -((i : ℤ) - P) - 1 = (P - 1) - (i : ℤ) from by ring, smul_smul]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl hterm, ← Finset.sum_smul,
    cbz_vandermonde_top (k + (m : ℤ)) (by omega) (-(k + (m : ℤ) - (N : ℤ))) (P - 1),
    show (k + (m : ℤ)) + (-(k + (m : ℤ) - (N : ℤ))) = (N : ℤ) from by ring]

/-- The vacuum residue in the right slot, for **every** `u : 𝒱` (the scalar `C(N,P−1)` does not
depend on the weight, so the homogeneous case extends by linearity). -/
theorem mkAnmFull_resHom_vacuum (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m : ℕ) (P : ℤ) (u : 𝒱) :
    mkAnmFull W N m (resHom W (m : ℤ) P u W.vacuum)
      = cbz (N : ℤ) (P - 1) • mkAnmFull W N m u := by
  refine reduce_homogeneous W
    (P := fun u => mkAnmFull W N m (resHom W (m : ℤ) P u W.vacuum)
      = cbz (N : ℤ) (P - 1) • mkAnmFull W N m u) ?_ ?_ ?_ u
  · intro k a ha
    exact mkAnmFull_resHom_vacuum_homog W N m P ha
  · show mkAnmFull W N m (resHom W (m : ℤ) P 0 W.vacuum)
        = cbz (N : ℤ) (P - 1) • mkAnmFull W N m 0
    simp only [resHom_zero_left_dj, map_zero, smul_zero]
  · intro x y hx hy
    replace hx : mkAnmFull W N m (resHom W (m : ℤ) P x W.vacuum)
        = cbz (N : ℤ) (P - 1) • mkAnmFull W N m x := hx
    replace hy : mkAnmFull W N m (resHom W (m : ℤ) P y W.vacuum)
        = cbz (N : ℤ) (P - 1) • mkAnmFull W N m y := hy
    show mkAnmFull W N m (resHom W (m : ℤ) P (x + y) W.vacuum)
        = cbz (N : ℤ) (P - 1) • mkAnmFull W N m (x + y)
    rw [resHom_add_left, map_add, map_add, hx, hy, smul_add]

/-- **The vacuum in the RIGHT slot of `∗^N_{m,p}`, at general base level `m`**:
`[u ∗^N_{m,p} 𝟙] = C(p − m − 1, p − m)·[u]` in `A_{N,m}(𝒱)`, for every `u : 𝒱`.

The exact mirror of `anmGen_vacuum_scalar` (vacuum in the LEFT slot).  Rewriting
`(−1)^i C(m+N−p+i, i) = C(−(m+N−p)−1, i)` (`cbz_neg_upper`) and
`C(N, m+N−p+i) = C(N, (p−m)−i)` (`ZhuMu.cbz_symm`) turns the outer `i`-sum into a Vandermonde
convolution evaluating to `C(p−m−1, p−m)`.  Note the scalar is independent of the target `N`. -/
theorem mkAnmFull_anmGen_vacuum_right (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m p : ℕ) (u : 𝒱) :
    mkAnmFull W N m (anmGen W N m p u W.vacuum)
      = cbz ((p : ℤ) - (m : ℤ) - 1) ((p : ℤ) - (m : ℤ)) • mkAnmFull W N m u := by
  rw [anmGen, map_sum]
  have hsq : ∀ i : ℕ, ((-1 : ℂ) ^ i) * ((-1 : ℂ) ^ i) = 1 := by
    intro i; rw [← mul_pow]; norm_num
  have hterm : ∀ i ∈ Finset.range (p + 1),
      mkAnmFull W N m (((-1 : ℂ) ^ i * cbz ((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ) + (i : ℤ)) (i : ℤ))
          • resHom W (m : ℤ) ((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ) + (i : ℤ) + 1) u W.vacuum)
        = (cbz (-((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ)) - 1) (i : ℤ)
            * cbz (N : ℤ) (((p : ℤ) - (m : ℤ)) - (i : ℤ))) • mkAnmFull W N m u := by
    intro i _
    rw [map_smul, mkAnmFull_resHom_vacuum W N m _ u, smul_smul]
    congr 1
    have h1 : cbz ((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ) + (i : ℤ)) (i : ℤ)
        = (-1 : ℂ) ^ i * cbz (-((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ)) - 1) (i : ℤ) := by
      rw [cbz_neg_upper ((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ) + (i : ℤ)) i]
      congr 2
      ring
    have h2 : cbz (N : ℤ) ((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ) + (i : ℤ) + 1 - 1)
        = cbz (N : ℤ) (((p : ℤ) - (m : ℤ)) - (i : ℤ)) := by
      rw [show ((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ) + (i : ℤ) + 1 - 1)
            = (m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ) + (i : ℤ) from by ring,
        _root_.ZhuMu.cbz_symm N ((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ) + (i : ℤ))]
      congr 1
      ring
    rw [h1, h2, ← mul_assoc, hsq i, one_mul]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl hterm, ← Finset.sum_smul,
    ZhuRes.vandermonde_range (-((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ)) - 1) (N : ℤ)
      ((p : ℤ) - (m : ℤ)) (N := p + 1) (by push_cast; omega),
    show (-((m : ℤ) + (N : ℤ) - (p : ℤ)) - 1) + (N : ℤ) = (p : ℤ) - (m : ℤ) - 1 from by ring]

/-- **Dong–Jiang's unit law `u ∗ⁿ_m 𝟙 = u`** (the identity the generation sentence of DJ Thm 4.10
uses): the identity `𝟙` of `A_m(𝒱)` acts as the identity on `A_{N,m}(𝒱)` through the right action
`∗^N_m = ∗^N_{m,m}`.  Scalar `C(−1, 0) = 1`. -/
theorem mkAnmFull_anmRight_vacuum_right (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m : ℕ) (u : 𝒱) :
    mkAnmFull W N m (anmRight W N m u W.vacuum) = mkAnmFull W N m u := by
  rw [← anmGen_eq_anmRight, mkAnmFull_anmGen_vacuum_right,
    show ((m : ℤ) - (m : ℤ)) = 0 from by ring, show (0 : ℤ) - 1 = -1 from by ring,
    cbz_zero, one_smul]

/-- The vacuum in the right slot of the LEFT action `∗̄^N_m = ∗^N_{m,N}`:
`[u ∗̄^N_m 𝟙] = C(N − m − 1, N − m)·[u]`. -/
theorem mkAnmFull_anmGenBar_vacuum_right (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (N m : ℕ) (u : 𝒱) :
    mkAnmFull W N m (anmGenBar W N m u W.vacuum)
      = cbz ((N : ℤ) - (m : ℤ) - 1) ((N : ℤ) - (m : ℤ)) • mkAnmFull W N m u := by
  rw [anmGenBar, mkAnmFull_anmGen_vacuum_right]

/-- ⚠ **`u ∗̄^N_m 𝟙 = 0` for `N ≠ m`.**  Dong–Jiang's Thm 4.10 sentence writes `∗̄ⁿ_m` where the
argument needs `∗ⁿ_m`; this theorem is the certificate that the literal reading is false off the
diagonal, so the `∗̄` there is a typo (their parenthetical "`1 ∈ A_m(V)`" gives the right
reading). -/
theorem mkAnmFull_anmGenBar_vacuum_offdiag (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) {N m : ℕ} (h : N ≠ m)
    (u : 𝒱) : mkAnmFull W N m (anmGenBar W N m u W.vacuum) = 0 := by
  rw [mkAnmFull_anmGenBar_vacuum_right]
  rcases lt_or_gt_of_ne h with hlt | hgt
  · rw [cbz_apply_neg _ (by omega), zero_smul]
  · rw [cbz_lt (by omega) (by omega), zero_smul]

/-- On the diagonal `N = m` the two products agree and `[u ∗̄^m_m 𝟙] = [u]`. -/
theorem mkAnmFull_anmGenBar_vacuum_diag (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (m : ℕ) (u : 𝒱) :
    mkAnmFull W m m (anmGenBar W m m u W.vacuum) = mkAnmFull W m m u := by
  rw [anmGen_diag_eq, mkAnmFull_anmRight_vacuum_right]

/-! ## §4 Generation of `M(U)` by its level-`m` piece -/

section Generation

variable {W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱} {m : ℕ}

/-- The distinguished level-`m` vectors of `M(U)`: `𝟙 ⊗ w` for `w ∈ U`. -/
noncomputable def djVacTensor (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (U : AmMod W m) (w : U.carrier) :
    DJCarrier W U :=
  DJCarrier.incl W U m (mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m W.vacuum ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w))

theorem djVacTensor_def (U : AmMod W m) (w : U.carrier) :
    djVacTensor W U w
      = DJCarrier.incl W U m (mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m W.vacuum ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w)) := rfl

theorem djVacTensor_mem_degM (U : AmMod W m) (w : U.carrier) :
    djVacTensor W U w ∈ DJCarrier.deg W U m :=
  ⟨mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m W.vacuum ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w), rfl⟩

/-- **Every level-`m` elementary tensor is a vacuum tensor** — unconditionally.  `[x] ⊗ w =
𝟙 ⊗ ρ([x])·w` by the balancing plus the sharp Frenkel–Zhu unit `𝟙 ∗^m_m x = x`. -/
theorem mkDJPiece_eq_vacuum_tmul (U : AmMod W m) (x : 𝒱) (w : U.carrier) :
    mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m x ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w)
      = mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m W.vacuum ⊗ₜ[ℂ] U.ρ (mkAnFull W m x) w) := by
  have h := mkDJPiece_balance U m W.vacuum x w
  rwa [anmRight_diag_vacuum_left] at h

/-- **`M(U)(m)` is spanned by the vacuum tensors `𝟙 ⊗ w`** — unconditionally (no `DJAnnEqAn`). -/
theorem djCarrier_degM_le_span (U : AmMod W m) :
    DJCarrier.deg W U m ≤ Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (djVacTensor W U)) := by
  intro z hz
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hz
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := mkDJPiece_surjective U m x
  induction y using TensorProduct.induction_on with
  | zero =>
      simp only [map_zero]
      exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | tmul t w =>
      refine Submodule.Quotient.induction_on _ t fun v => ?_
      show DJCarrier.incl W U m (mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m v ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w))
        ∈ Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (djVacTensor W U))
      rw [mkDJPiece_eq_vacuum_tmul U v w]
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨U.ρ (mkAnFull W m v) w, rfl⟩
  | add y₁ y₂ h₁ h₂ =>
      rw [map_add, map_add]
      exact Submodule.add_mem _ h₁ h₂

/-- **A `𝒱`-submodule of `M(U)`**: a `ℂ`-subspace stable under every Dong–Jiang mode `u_p`. -/
def DJModeStable (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (U : AmMod W m) (hD : DJActionDescent W m)
    (S : Submodule ℂ (DJCarrier W U)) : Prop :=
  ∀ (p : ℤ) (a : 𝒱), ∀ x ∈ S, djMode W U hD p a x ∈ S

/-- **One mode application reaches level `n` from level `m`.**  For homogeneous `v ∈ 𝒱_k`,
`v_{k−1+m−n} (𝟙 ⊗ w) = (v ∗ⁿ_{m,m} 𝟙) ⊗ w = [v] ⊗ w`.  This *is* Dong–Jiang's one-line generation
argument: the unit law `mkAnmFull_anmRight_vacuum_right` evaluates the product.  No induction on
the level. -/
theorem djMode_vacTensor (U : AmMod W m) (hD : DJActionDescent W m) {k : ℤ} {v : 𝒱}
    (hv : v ∈ W.grading k) (n : ℕ) (w : U.carrier) :
    djMode W U hD (k - 1 + (m : ℤ) - (n : ℤ)) v (djVacTensor W U w)
      = DJCarrier.incl W U n (mkDJPiece W U n (mkAnmFull W n m v ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w)) := by
  have hN : muTargetLevel k (k - 1 + (m : ℤ) - (n : ℤ)) m = (n : ℤ) := by
    simp only [muTargetLevel]; ring
  have h := djMode_apply_tmul U hD (k - 1 + (m : ℤ) - (n : ℤ)) hv hN W.vacuum w
  rw [djVacTensor_def, h, anmGen_eq_anmRight, mkAnmFull_anmRight_vacuum_right]

/-- **Dong–Jiang Theorem 4.10, generation clause (sharp form).**  A mode-stable subspace of
`M(U)` containing the vacuum tensors `𝟙 ⊗ w` (`w ∈ U`) is all of `M(U)`.

DJ's one line, verbatim: an element of `M(U) = ⨁ₙ M(U)(n)` is a finite sum of vectors `[v] ⊗ w`,
and `[v] ⊗ w = v_{wt v − 1 + m − n}(𝟙 ⊗ w)` by the unit law `v ∗ⁿ_m 𝟙 = v`.  **No induction on the
level.**  The only hypothesis is the mode descent `hD` (DJ Lemma 2.8). -/
theorem djCarrier_generated_by_vacTensor (U : AmMod W m) (hD : DJActionDescent W m)
    (S : Submodule ℂ (DJCarrier W U)) (hS : DJModeStable W U hD S)
    (hvac : ∀ w : U.carrier, djVacTensor W U w ∈ S) : S = ⊤ := by
  have hlevel : ∀ (n : ℕ) (x : DJPiece W U n), DJCarrier.incl W U n x ∈ S := by
    intro n x
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := mkDJPiece_surjective U n x
    induction y using TensorProduct.induction_on with
    | zero =>
        simp only [map_zero]
        exact Submodule.zero_mem _
    | tmul t w =>
        refine Submodule.Quotient.induction_on _ t fun v => ?_
        show DJCarrier.incl W U n (mkDJPiece W U n (mkAnmFull W n m v ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w)) ∈ S
        refine reduce_homogeneous W
          (P := fun v =>
            DJCarrier.incl W U n (mkDJPiece W U n (mkAnmFull W n m v ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w)) ∈ S) ?_ ?_ ?_ v
        · intro k a ha
          rw [← djMode_vacTensor U hD ha n w]
          exact hS _ _ _ (hvac w)
        · simp only [map_zero, TensorProduct.zero_tmul]
          exact Submodule.zero_mem _
        · intro x₁ x₂ h₁ h₂
          simp only [map_add, TensorProduct.add_tmul]
          exact Submodule.add_mem _ h₁ h₂
    | add y₁ y₂ h₁ h₂ =>
        rw [map_add, map_add]
        exact Submodule.add_mem _ h₁ h₂
  rw [eq_top_iff]
  intro z _
  refine DirectSum.induction_on z (Submodule.zero_mem _) ?_
    (fun x y hx hy => Submodule.add_mem _ hx hy)
  intro n x
  exact hlevel n x

/-- **Dong–Jiang Theorem 4.10, generation clause**: `M(U)` is generated by its level-`m` piece
`M(U)(m) = A_{m,m}(𝒱) ⊗_{A_m(𝒱)} U`.  Any `𝒱`-submodule of `M(U)` containing `M(U)(m)` is
`M(U)`. -/
theorem djCarrier_generated_by_degM (U : AmMod W m) (hD : DJActionDescent W m)
    (S : Submodule ℂ (DJCarrier W U)) (hS : DJModeStable W U hD S)
    (hm : DJCarrier.deg W U m ≤ S) : S = ⊤ :=
  djCarrier_generated_by_vacTensor U hD S hS (fun w => hm (djVacTensor_mem_degM U w))

/-- The same, as "the `𝒱`-submodule generated by `M(U)(m)` is `M(U)`": the infimum of all
mode-stable subspaces containing `M(U)(m)` is `⊤`. -/
theorem djCarrier_iInf_modeStable_degM (U : AmMod W m) (hD : DJActionDescent W m) :
    (⨅ S ∈ {S : Submodule ℂ (DJCarrier W U) |
        DJModeStable W U hD S ∧ DJCarrier.deg W U m ≤ S}, S) = ⊤ := by
  refine le_antisymm le_top (le_iInf₂ fun S hS => ?_)
  obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := hS
  rw [djCarrier_generated_by_degM U hD S h1 h2]

end Generation

/-! ## §5 The unconditional base level `m = 0` -/

/-- **Generation at base level `m = 0`, hypothesis-free.**  At `m = 0` the mode descent is the
theorem `djActionDescent_zero`, so `M(U)` is generated by `M(U)(0)` with no hypothesis at all. -/
theorem djCarrier_generated_by_degZero (W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱) (U : AmMod W 0)
    (S : Submodule ℂ (DJCarrier W U)) (hS : DJModeStable W U (djActionDescent_zero W) S)
    (hm : DJCarrier.deg W U 0 ≤ S) : S = ⊤ :=
  djCarrier_generated_by_degM U (djActionDescent_zero W) S hS hm

/-! ## §6 Dong–Jiang's own phrasing: generated by `U` (this is where Prop. `pa4.5` enters) -/

section GeneratedByU

variable {W : VertexOperatorAlgebra 𝒱} {m : ℕ}

/-- Under DJ Prop. `pa4.5`, the level-`m` isomorphism `M(U)(m) ≅ U` carries `w ∈ U` back to the
vacuum tensor `𝟙 ⊗ w`. -/
theorem degMEquiv_symm_eq_vacTensor (h : DJAnnEqAn W m) (U : AmMod W m) (w : U.carrier) :
    (((DJCarrier.degMEquiv W m h U).symm w : DJCarrier.deg W U m) : DJCarrier W U)
      = djVacTensor W U w := by
  have key : DJCarrier.degMEquiv W m h U
      ⟨DJCarrier.incl W U m (mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m W.vacuum ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w)),
        ⟨mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m W.vacuum ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w), rfl⟩⟩ = w := by
    rw [DJCarrier.degMEquiv_incl_tmul, U.ρ_one, Module.End.one_apply]
  have hsymm : (DJCarrier.degMEquiv W m h U).symm w
      = ⟨DJCarrier.incl W U m (mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m W.vacuum ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w)),
          ⟨mkDJPiece W U m (mkAnmFull W m m W.vacuum ⊗ₜ[ℂ] w), rfl⟩⟩ := by
    rw [LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq]
    exact key.symm
  rw [hsymm]
  rfl

/-- **Dong–Jiang Theorem 4.10's sentence, verbatim**: "`M(U)` is generated by
`U ≅ A_{m,m}(V) ⊗_{A_m(V)} U` by Proposition `pa4.5`".  Given DJ Prop. `pa4.5`
(`h : DJAnnEqAn W m`), a `𝒱`-submodule of `M(U)` containing the image of `U` under the level-`m`
isomorphism is all of `M(U)`. -/
theorem djCarrier_generated_by_U (h : DJAnnEqAn W m) (U : AmMod W m)
    (hD : DJActionDescent W m) (S : Submodule ℂ (DJCarrier W U)) (hS : DJModeStable W U hD S)
    (hU : ∀ w : U.carrier,
      (((DJCarrier.degMEquiv W m h U).symm w : DJCarrier.deg W U m) : DJCarrier W U) ∈ S) :
    S = ⊤ := by
  refine djCarrier_generated_by_vacTensor U hD S hS fun w => ?_
  rw [← degMEquiv_symm_eq_vacTensor h U w]
  exact hU w

end GeneratedByU

